{
  "what": "The deleted occurrences a series keeps when \"this and all following\" writes it from the cut on: cal_core::tail_exceptions, row by row. Read by the core's own test, by the phone's door test in cal-ffi, and by the TypeScript contract test through the WebAssembly door.",
  "why": "Decisions 152 (a deletion keeps its place when every occurrence moves with the start, by one and the same step in the rule's unit: days, months or years), 188 (with a new rule it keeps its day, only where the new rule still meets it; a new end or another spelling is no new rule), 189 (a rule that names its days moves with the date of \"this and all following\", and its deletions keep their places; one that did not move keeps its days, and so do its deletions) and 196 (a rule the user set that is the moved rule is that move). Every instant here is the shell's expansion as a Berlin device writes it; the core reads no clock, so the days come with them, on the series' own clock and on the device's.",
